== the verdict
   -> NO RETURN: some tsens zone did not come back to within 0.5 C of its own window A reading
      within 240s (the largest difference was 4.1 C BELOW window A's reading of the SAME zone), so window C would not
      have read window A's state -- it would have read whatever the run did to the phone after A.
      This run therefore PRINTS NO PRICE for the second heat cause, and that is the correct answer:
      the number the old design would have printed from A and B alone (the largest warming above) is
      not the governor's cost, it is the governor's cost PLUS however far the phone moved on its own
      -- and this instrument has just measured that the phone moved further than it can resolve.

   What this run DOES establish is about the phone: after the intervention was undone, the zones were
   still 4.1 C away from their window A readings 240s later. That is the number a
   longer wait or a bigger margin would have to beat, and it is printed with the setting that produced
   it.

   The cores read 'interactive' cpu0=interactive cpu1=interactive cpu2=interactive cpu3=interactive -- the state it started in.

   --keep: this run's scratch directory is /tmp/zl1-governor-temp-ab.ubXCQ9 (deltas, deltas.note, win.A/B/C, back).

